Z||000004||fierospeeder||02-17-2001||05:34 AM||||Im going to look at it today.  If it says no right turn while pedestrians are present then im going to court with this.  <P>I seen "Matlock" try to fight his ticket when he didn't see a stop sign because a bush was blocking his view of it.  He did lose and lost his money for the rental of a camcorder which he was taping other drivers failing to stop.  Well, i need to watch something at 3am.<P>I wasn't even speeding and thats what PO me so much.  And this jag couldn't have given me a warning.  Right off the bat, i can tell he was ticket happy.  I share the same zip code with this town and its 1 mile away from my house.  This is the 2nd time i have gotten a ticket from them.  <P>I know other people in here mentioned they have been pulled over because of the kind of car they drive or how they look.  I think i should get a ford escort.  I guess this just makes me hate 90% of cops now.  I have met some kewl cops that let me have warnings and what happened to the old saying "tell the cop the truth" guess it doesn't work.  Well thats what i see on cops, but there on camera.<P>If those no turn on red signs expire after 8pm i have a case, or if i can see if a street light is out i know i can use that because i didn't see that sign.  Judge Dred would probably let me go, aka stallone.<P>Also, if you lose in court what does happen to you?||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-17-2001||11:19 AM||||usually you have to pay the court costs. But the fine is usually less. If you win you pay notta. Ive been stopped just for having a red sports car I think, the ticket is usually bogus. I had one stop me in Granville Oh, a small college town, just because he wasnt used to seeing Ferraris in town, figured it was stolen.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou_dias||02-19-2001||01:03 PM||||I like the time that I was doing 65 (the speed limit) on the highway in the rightmost lane of a 3 lane highway and a statey is crusing up on the left most lane and flashes his light straight across to me to warn me I'm going too fast.  Frag all these aceholes already.  Talk about racism, this is carism.<P>Then there's the time I'm doing 50 in a 65 on this same highway.  It had stopped snowing 5 hours before and the damn cheap-as state hadn't used my tax money to plow the highway yet and I switch lanes and since my car is low to the ground, the snow that was built up between lanes as I tried switching got underneath my right side and caused me to do a couple of 360's and I ended up in a slight muddy ditch and had to be pulled out.  Along comes a state-anus and gives me a $75 for driving at an unreasonable speed even though all he saw was me on the side of the road.  What an attitude on him too.<BR>Ofcourse I had to be driving poorly, I own a cheap red sports car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BN Boomer||02-20-2001||01:24 PM||||The problem with these "I got a ticket" stories is that they are too one sided. No offense, but everyone seems to think that they are totally innocent and behaved like a respectful little angel when stopped. I guess I'm just a little too skeptical.<P>I got a lot of tickets when I was younger. I had to go some sort of "Traffic School" as well. My insurance cost me fortune. The only one of those tickets that I truly did not deserve I took to court and got it thrown out. Not that I was blatantly rude or disrepectful, but I can't help but think that if I had had a better attitude and demeanor most of the time I would not have been issued quite as many citations. I believe that cops pick up on quite a few things, honesty and sincerity being a couple of them. Of course there will always be the occassional *******  cop, but I still think they are the exception rather than the rule. <P>I've been pulled over 3 times in the last year in my red 85 GT. Once for doing 50 in a 40, once for passing in a turn lane instead of turning, and once for doing 75 in a 60. Not one of these stops resulted in a citation. I think how you handle the situation plays a big part in the outcome.||||reg||1
